WEBVTT

00:05:58.796 --> 00:06:01.316
Now two years later, Whitney,

00:06:01.356 --> 00:06:03.476
we haven't passed
the Marshall Plan for Moms.

00:06:03.476 --> 00:06:06.476
And what I mean by that is we haven't
passed any of the tenets.

00:06:06.516 --> 00:06:07.916
We haven't passed paid leave,

00:06:07.956 --> 00:06:09.876
we haven't passed affordable childcare,

00:06:09.916 --> 00:06:12.396
and we let the child tax credit expire.

00:06:12.436 --> 00:06:14.356
So we've bailed out airlines.

00:06:15.276 --> 00:06:16.996
But we haven’t bailed out moms.

00:06:17.756 --> 00:06:21.356
And, you know, for me as an activist,
as a social entrepreneur,

00:06:21.396 --> 00:06:24.396
looking at this is devastating,

00:06:24.396 --> 00:06:25.556
because in many ways,

00:06:25.596 --> 00:06:28.356
you're waiting for Congress
to grow a heart.

00:06:28.396 --> 00:06:30.756
You know, if there was ever
going to be a moment